- L3: (2,3)-(4,1) slope = (1-3)/(4-2) = -2/2 = -1, not allowed. So can't.\n- L3: (2,3)-(3,1) slope = (1-3)/(3-2) = -2, allowed. Covers (2,3),(3,1).\n- L4: (2,4)-(3,2) slope = (2-4)/(3-2) = -2, allowed. Covers (2,4),(3,2).\n\nNow we have covered points:\n\n- (2,1) L1\n- (2,2) L2\n- (2,3) L3\n- (2,4) L4\n- (3,1) L3\n- (3,2) L4\n- (3,3) not covered\n- (4,1) not covered\n- (4,2) L1\n- (5,1) L2\n\nRemaining points: (3,3) and (4,1). We have used all 4 lines. Could we adjust to include them? Perhaps we can modify L1 to also include (4,1) instead of (4,2). Let's try L1: (2,1)-(4,1) slope = (1-1)/(4-2) = 0, horizontal, not allowed. So can't.\n\nMaybe L1: (2,1)-(3,3) slope = (3-1)/(3-2) = 2, allowed. That would cover (2,1) and (3,3). Then we need to cover (4,2) elsewhere. Let's try to reassign.\n\nLet's try a new assignment:\n\n- L1: (2,1)-(3,3) slope = 2, allowed. Covers (2,1),(3,3).\n- L2: (2,2)-(5,1) slope = -1/3, allowed. Covers (2,2),(5,1).\n- L3: (2,3)-(4,2) slope = (2-3)/(4-2) = -1/2, allowed. Covers (2,3),(4,2).\n- L4: (2,4)-(3,2) slope = (2-4)/(3-2) = -2, allowed. Covers (2,4),(3,2).\n\nNow covered points:\n\n- (2,1) L1\n- (2,2) L2\n- (2,3) L3\n- (2,4) L4\n- (3,1) not covered\n- (3,2) L4\n- (3,3) L1\n- (4,1) not covered\n- (4,2) L3\n- (5,1) L2\n\nRemaining: (3,1) and (4,1). Could we adjust L2 to also cover (3,1)? L2 currently (2,2)-(5,1). Does (3,1) lie on that line? Let's check: slope = -1/3. Equation: y - 2 = -1/3 (x-2). For x=3, y = 2 - 1/3 = 5/3 ≈ 1.666, not 1. So (3,1) not on L2. Could we modify L2 to be (2,2)-(4,1)? Slope = (1-2)/(4-2) = -1/2, allowed. That would cover (2,2),(4,1). Then (5,1) would be uncovered. But maybe we can cover (5,1) with another line, maybe L3 or L4. Let's try:\n\n- L1: (2,1)-(3,3) slope 2 (covers (2,1),(3,3))\n- L2: (2,2)-(4,1) slope -1/2 (covers (2,2),(4,1))\n- L3: (2,3)-(5,1) slope -2/3 (covers (2,3),(5,1))\n- L4: (2,4)-(3,2) slope -2 (covers (2,4),(3,2))\n\nNow covered:\n\n- (2,1) L1\n- (2,2) L2\n- (2,3) L3\n- (2,4) L4\n- (3,1) not 